<h1>About me</h1>

<p>
Hi, my name is Denni. I'm a research associate and I work in a structured, analytical and reliable way.
Alongside my job, I help people turn complex material into something understandable and reach solid results – fully remote.
As a PhD candidate in 3D printing, I tutor STEM subjects (mathematics, computer science, natural sciences and engineering).
As a research associate, I have been teaching master's and bachelor's students in engineering subjects for more than a year.
This includes running tutorials, giving guest lectures, organising courses and writing exams.
Especially because I write exams myself, I can put myself in the shoes of your upcoming exam
and give you tips on what really matters in the end.
</p>
